hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"259","We have Bandar, we have Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi, we have Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qais, he said: I asked Aisha, may God be pleased with her God Almighty: How was the sleep of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during ritual impurity? She said: “He did all of that: sometimes he washed and slept, and sometimes he performed ablution and slept.” Nasr bin Bahr Al-Khawlani narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Muawiyah bin Salih narrated to me, that Abdullah bin Abi Qais narrated to him, Likewise, he said: “Perhaps he performed ablution and went to sleep before he washed himself,” so I said: Praise be to God who made the matter sufficient."
